    "intent": "DELIVER",
    "body": "## Episode conclusion (advisory, not acceptance)\n\nIntent: DELIVER\nStatement: Reproduced the remaining 21a5 delivery-record gap and fixed it at direct commit ba7690a. In the sealed case-1/case-2 replay, the guard's refreshed conclusion still named all five historical artifacts in `artifacts`; a consumer counting the refreshed record's named paths therefore saw `delivered:true, recorded:[]` even though `MAINTENANCE-REVIEW.md` was present at the expected commit with canonical detail and the full prior provenance was carried. The guard now names only the changed/added paths in the refreshed conclusion, keeps unchanged prior artifacts in `check.artifacts` at their original delivery commit with a carried label, and recovers known prior paths from both fields when deciding whether a later direct advance touched an artifact. Verification: the sealed delivery-record oracle reproduces `delivered:true, recorded:[]` on pre-fix 21a5 with four false checks and passes 28/28 on ba7690a; all 11 maintenance oracles pass; the six related suites pass 55/55; `tsc -b` and the public-API baseline pass. Limit: this makes the product's refreshed record name one new delivery correctly; it does not make a fixed executor call `conclude`, does not accept or promote anything, and leaves the canonical head and operator authority unchanged.\nArtifacts:\n- src/deployment/direct_delivery_guard.ts\n- src/project_continuity/episode.ts\n- test/pnwf_direct_guard.test.ts\n- scripts/pnwf/software/self-maintenance-delivery-record.mjs\n- scripts/pnwf/software/self-maintenance-late-guard.mjs\n- scripts/pnwf/software/self-maintenance-prepared-ref.mjs\n- scripts/pnwf/software/self-maintenance-sealed-guard.mjs\nWaiting on: (none)\nNext step: (none)\nEvidence: (none)\nBasis: revision 0, head 082f77a9a4602d1eb5a2d9be1260186fa41c4a61\nArtifact provenance:\n- src/deployment/direct_delivery_guard.ts: present=true tracked=true committed=true source=WORKTREE digest=5ed16e49b361 commit=ba7690ab3da6\n- s